  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Atlantic Diving Supply has $4.5B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Atlantic Diving Supply recorded 60,859 awards so far this fiscal year, with an average award size of $73.8K. Atlantic Diving Supply's obligations fell 25.0% year over year. Department of Defense is the dominant buyer, awarding $4.3B in obligations to Atlantic Diving Supply in FY2026 to date. General Services Administration, Department of Homeland Security, and the Department of Justice round out the next largest agency relationships, at $96.1M, $56.5M, and $28.7M respectively. Service Establishment Equipment and Supplies Merchant Wholesalers and All Other Miscellaneous Manufacturing are the largest NAICS markets for Atlantic Diving Supply, at $2.6B and $1.3B respectively. Atlantic Diving Supply also received awards in manufacturing and medical supply categories, including Bare Printed Circuit Board Manufacturing at $111M and Surgical Appliance and Supplies Manufacturing at $30.7M. Atlantic Diving Supply's current-year totals are partial, covering fiscal year to date, and award-value figures in some tables represent total contract values rather than single-year obligations.",
